'''Thresh Point + Ahri Assist:'''
<section begin="Ahri"/>
Thresh can easily use Ahri's [[Ahri#Foxfire Rain Assist|Foxfire Rain Assist]] ({{input|4T}}) to fill the gap between {{input|5H}}>{{input|5[S1]}}, allowing for a true blockstring into charged [[Thresh#Death Sentence|Death Sentence]] ({{input|5[S1]}}) from which he can do a high-low mixup with {{input|j.5H}} and {{input|j.6H}}.

[[Ahri#Foxfire Rain Assist|Foxfire Rain]] is also a fantastic assist to use for left-right mixups with Thresh's teleporting [[Thresh#Step Dash|Step Dash]], since it is a series of projectiles and thus much less vulnerable to Parry from the opponent compared to most other assists.

With {{fi|2X Assist}}, Thresh can get a blockstring into {{input|5[S1]}} and still have assist available for gapless high-low mix or a surprise teleport cross-up. During neutral, calling Ahri’s [[Ahri#Spirit Rush Assist|Spirit Rush Assist]] ({{input|5T}} twice can allow her to move into position to start offense while the opponent is dealing with Thresh’s zoning, especially if they jump. While somewhat slow, Ahri’s {{input|5T}}>{{input|4T}} provides a very active attack just beyond the reach of Thresh’s {{input|5H}}, and is very good at catching the opponent’s assist calls and putting them on cooldown.

Ahri is very good at using [[Thresh#Lantern Tag|Lantern Tag]] thanks to her strong mixup options when in the air. If Thresh cancels any of his heavy normals into Lantern Tag and the opponent is standing, Ahri can true blockstring with her {{input|j.2L}} and go for a number of different mixup options from there (e.g. {{input|j.2L}}>{{input|j.L}}>airdash {{input|j.L}}, {{input|j.2L}}>{{input|j.L}}>{{input|j.L}}>land,{{input|j.2L}}>{{input|j.M}}>land). If you have to Lantern Tag when the opponent is crouch blocking, Ahri can use her airdash to bait the opponent's {{input|2H}} or Parry and punish.
<section end="Ahri"/>

