== Combo List ==
=== Combo Theory ===
This section is HEAVILY WIP.


When not using assists Illaoi's goal is to get a tentacle onto the field to allow her to start her strike-throw mix and to jail opponents with riskier block strings.


To this end, Illaoi wants to be ending her combos with any of her {{input|S2}} buttons as they all create tentacles with the most common option being {{input|j.S2}}.


==== One Tentacle ====
Midscreen:
WIP.

Corner:
If you are able to start a combo with one (1) tentacle present, you can go into a higher damage combo that uses that tentacle later or add it's use as a extension to the front of existing combos.


The basic extension is using {{Input| 2M/5M > 6S1~5S1, 5M}} at the start of a combo with a few things to keep in mind depending on if you want to go into {{input|2S2}} or {{input|2S2}}.


For combos that use {{input|2S2}}, you can use three (3) {{input|M}} buttons, two (2) {{input|H}} buttons, and {{input|6S1~5S1}} before the {{input|2S2}} will be blockable due to a 1 frame gap.
This gap is extremely punishing as you aren't pushed back by {{input|2S2}} and are left -6.


For combos that use {{input|5S2}}, you can use two (2) {{input|M}} buttons, one (1) {{input|H}} button, and {{input|6S1~5S1}} to maintain the same recovery height for the opponent. You can use up to two (2) more {{input|M}} buttons and one (1) more {{input|5H}} button with each one added increasing the height the opponent recovers at. With a total of six (6) {{input|M and H}} buttons used, you will need to jump after the opponent in order to continue the combos as the opponent recovers before you would be able to hit with {{input|5M}} or {{input|5H}}

